#: ../../source/contributing.md:62
msgid "Commit message prefixes:"
msgstr "Préfixes de message de commit :"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:64
msgid "`feat:` New feature"
msgstr "`feat:` Nouvelle fonctionnalité"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:65
msgid "`fix:` Bug fix"
msgstr "`fix:` Correction de bug"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:66
msgid "`docs:` Documentation"
msgstr "`docs:` Documentation"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:67
msgid "`style:` Formatting or code style"
msgstr "`style:` Formatage ou style de code"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:68
msgid "`refactor:` Refactoring"
msgstr "`refactor:` Refactorisation"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:69
msgid "`test:` Adding tests"
msgstr "`test:` Ajout de tests"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:70
msgid "`chore:` Maintenance tasks"
msgstr "`chore:` Tâches de maintenance"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:72
msgid "6. Push and Open a Pull Request"
msgstr "6. Pusher et créer une Pull Request"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:78
msgid "Then open a PR on GitHub."
msgstr "Puis créer une PR sur GitHub."

#: ../../source/contributing.md:80
msgid "Development Guidelines"
msgstr "Directives de développement"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:82
msgid "Code Style"
msgstr "Style de code"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:84
msgid "Follow PEP 8 for Python code"
msgstr "Suivre PEP 8 pour le code Python"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:85
msgid "NumPy-style docstrings (required for numpydoc gate)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:86
msgid "Type hints everywhere (mypy strict)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:87
msgid "Maximum 88 characters per line (Black default)"
msgstr "Maximum 88 caractères par ligne (défaut de Black)"

#: ../../source/contributing.md ../../source/contributing.md:89
msgid "Tests"
msgstr "Tests"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:91
msgid "**Coverage target: 100%** (enforced via `fail_under=100` in CI)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:92
msgid ""
"No `# pragma: no cover` annotations — unreachable branches are handled "
"via `exclude_lines` in `pyproject.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:93
msgid "Use pytest for unit tests"
msgstr "Utiliser pytest pour les tests unitaires"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:94
msgid "Add doctests (`>>>`) for all public functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:96
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "Documentation"

#: ../../source/contributing.md:98
msgid "Document every new public function with NumPy-style docstrings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:99
msgid ""
"Include `Examples` section with `>>>` prompts in docstrings (collected by"
" `make doctest`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:100
msgid "Update the Sphinx docs in `docs/source/` when adding features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:101
msgid ""
"Use `from ketu.submodule import function` style — not `import ketu; "
"ketu.function()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:103
msgid "pyswisseph Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing.md:105
msgid ""
"`pyswisseph` is **test/validation only** — it is never imported at "
"runtime. Runtime code must be pure NumPy. This maintains AGPL isolation. "
"If a new calculation requires Swiss Ephemeris data, generate offline "
"coefficients (as was done for Chiron in v1.3) and embed them as `.npz` "
"files."
msgstr ""

